  <static seed="11">
    <statement><p>Find the derivative of <m>4x^{2} e^{-x}\text{.}</m></p>
<p><m>f'(x)=</m> <fillin characters="50" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\exp\mathopen{}\left(-x\right)\mathopen{}\left(8x^{1}-4x^{2}\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>Using the product rule and noting from the mini-chain rule that <m>\frac{d}{dx} e^{-x} = -e^{-x}\text{,}</m></p>
<p><me>\begin{aligned}
                            \frac{d}{dx} \left(4x^{2} e^{-x}\right) \amp = \left(\frac{d}{dx} 4x^{2}\right)\cdot e^{-x} + 4x^{2}\cdot \left(\frac{d}{dx} e^{-x}\right)\\
                            \amp = {8}x^{{1}} e^{-x} + 4x^{2}\left(-e^{-x}\right)\\
                            \amp =e^{-x}\left({8}x^{{1}} - 4x^{2}\right).
                        \end{aligned}</me></p>
</solution>
